%9Setting:%9

    show_names_on_join_limit (integer; default: 18, the Shellter default
    configuration sets 1)

%9Description:%9

    Limits the nick list that is printed when you join a channel.

    If the channel has more nicks than this, joining prints only the count
    line ("Total of N nicks ...") and not the table of nicks. 0 means no
    limit. The table is also left out when you are alone on the channel and
    show_names_on_join_alone is OFF (default: ON, the Shellter default
    configuration sets OFF); then only the count line is printed.

    Nothing is printed when show_names_on_join is OFF. The list can always
    be printed with /NAMES.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET show_names_on_join_limit 30
    /SET show_names_on_join_limit 0
    /SET show_names_on_join_alone on

%9See also:%9

    SET, NAMES, SHOW_NAMES_ON_JOIN, SHOW_NAMES_ON_JOIN_ALONE
